*   **Conclusion:** Your total itemizable deductions (around $6,900) are far below the $20,800 standard deduction. 

### 2. Home Office Deduction
*   **W-2 Job:** You cannot deduct home office expenses for your W-2 job.
*   **Consulting Business:** You **can** deduct home office expenses against your $15,000 self-employment income, provided the space is used *exclusively and regularly* for your consulting business.
*   **How to calculate:** 
    *   *Actual Expenses Method:* Your office is 20.3% of your apartment (140 sq ft / 690 sq ft). You can deduct 20.3% of your annual rent ($25,200/year × 20.3% = ~$5,115), plus 20.3% of utilities and internet.
