Because you have independent consulting income, you can claim a home office deduction against that specific income. You have two ways to calculate this:
*   **Actual Expenses Method:** Your office is 140 sq ft out of 690 sq ft, which is **20.29%** of your home. You can deduct 20.29% of your rent ($2,100 x 12 months = $25,200/year * 20.29% = **~$5,113**), plus 20.29% of your utilities and renter's insurance.
